messages:
maya: Heads up — noticed a weird pattern for streaming responses: sometimes the connection drops mid-stream and the SDK surfaces a generic Error('stream closed') with zero context. Hard to decide whether to retry, resume, or surface to users.

sam: Can you paste an example error payload / logs? is this on hosted or dedicated?

maya: Hosted. Logs show connection reset followed by a 200-ish final chunk sometimes, other times just EOF. Example server error blob we captured: 

```json
{
  \"type\": \"stream_interruption\", 
  \"http_status\": 499,
  \"message\": \"connection reset by peer while streaming tokens\",
  \"details\": null
}
```

No hint fields currently. SDK just throws generic "stream closed".

leo: 499 is messy since it's client-side but our infra surfaces it. For DX we should standardize a structured error envelope for streaming: typed_code, resumable(bool), retry_after(s), and a human hint.

shreya: Agree. Proposal (minimal): 
- typed_code: one of [StreamInterrupted, AuthFailure, RateLimited, InternalTransient]
- resumable: boolean (can client request resume with cursor/token?)
- retry_after_seconds: optional int
- hint: short sentence to show in logs/UX

Example new shape we could return: 
```json
{
  \"typed_code\": \"StreamInterrupted\",
  \"http_status\": 499,
  \"resumable\": true,
  \"resume_cursor\": \"at_token_1234\",
  \"retry_after_seconds\": 2,
  \"hint\": \"Transient network blip — resume using resume_cursor or retry with exponential backoff.\"
}
```

manuel: I like resume_cursor but only if replay/resume semantics are supported. For many models we can do prefix resume by re-sending cached KV prefix and a cursor index. If resumable=false, SDK should expose a clear typed exception so apps don't try naive retry.

maya: Exactly. Right now Go/JS SDKs both return a plain IOError. I propose we: 
1) Add a StreamInterruptedError (typed) with properties {resumable, retry_after, resume_cursor, hint} exposed on the error object.
2) Add helpers: isRetryable(err) and suggestedBackoff(err) in SDK.

sam: How would JS usage look?

shreya: Sketch: 
```js
try {
  const stream = client.responses.stream(...)
  for await (const chunk of stream) { /* render tokens */ }
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof StreamInterruptedError) {
    if (err.resumable) {
      // attempt resume
      client.responses.resume(err.resume_cursor)
    } else if (isRetryable(err)) {
      await sleep(suggestedBackoff(err))
      // retry from scratch
    } else {
      // bubble up
    }
  } else {
    throw err
  }
}
```

leo: For Go, make the type implement errors.Is so folks can do errors.Is(err, inference.ErrStreamInterrupted). Also include helper pkg inference/errutil for SuggestedBackoff(err).

maya: We should also update sample-apps so onboarding reproduces streaming blips and shows best-practice handling. Idea: add samples/streaming-resume-tester with a proxy that randomly drops TCP after N tokens to exercise resume flow.

ci-bot: test-runner queued: sample-apps/streaming-resume-tester integration on node14 scheduled.

sam: UX question — what should the console/docs show for errors? My thought: short hint + icon for resumable + a sample code snippet to copy. Keep human-facing message concise and non-technical when possible.

shreya: +1. Suggested doc copy for 1-line: \"Partial response due to transient network error. You can resume the response (recommended) or retry. See code samples under Streaming errors.\"

manuel: Action items: 
- @eng-runtime: add typed envelope and resume cursor support on streaming API (maya + leo pairing)
- @devex: update SDKs to surface typed exceptions and helpers (sam + shreya)
- @samples: add streaming-resume-tester and a README showing correct client behavior (maya)
- @docs: add short snippet and UX copy (shreya)

maya: I'll open PRs tonight for the sample-app and a minimal SDK change (JS). Will tag folks.

sam: Thanks — please include a small test in SDKs that asserts err.resumable !== undefined for stream drops so we don't regress.

leo: One more thought — map HTTP statuses: 401/403 -> AuthFailure typed, 429 -> RateLimited (include retry_after_seconds), 5xx -> InternalTransient (include request_id). We'll document mapping in the error contract doc.

maya: Great. If nobody objects I'll file a meta-ticket to track changes across runtime, sdk, samples, and docs. :+1:

manuel: No objections, go for it.

ci-bot: created issue RW-4567: standardize streaming error envelope and SDK typed exceptions (assigned maya).
